# wip — folio-worktable
#
#>plan_folio_worktable_wip
#:operation #!cache
#:fixity #!tending
#:layer #!pragmatics

@plan: ~"./PLAN.md"
@wip_notebook: ~"../../../.spw/conventions/wip-notebook.spw"
@folios: ~"../../../design/folios/index.html"
@calendar: ~"../../../design/experiments/folios/calendar/index.html"
@primes: ~"../../../design/experiments/folios/primes/index.html"
@seed_card: ~"../../../public/js/modules/cards/seed-card.js"

operation = "cache"
fixity = "tending"

^"stream"{
 >>[2026-10-12 10:59] verify — the release shelf (7a95da5b), the request card at #folio-request, the primes demo (8703ed24) and the calendar demo (27b616e8) are in the tree; since 2026-10-10 only copy and .spw headers touched the folio pages. The calendar demo is linked from the experiments shelf, not from /design/folios/, and waits on the creator's browser review, which is worth most before October ends. Forms, prices, shipping, the primes demo and the first card request stay the creator's calls.
 >>[2026-10-27 13:40] hygiene — the creator's question moves from ^"open" into the notebook as #>wonder_folio_worktable_calendar, with a guess on record, a read probe and an answer set, so npm run wonder shows it; the call stays the creator's.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:20] verify — Since the 2026-10-10 Status: the October drop page (2c95bf13), Honk Bazongas restored (5482751f), W44's five (5884cc59), tall scans whole on the plate (9571af62), clear-piece ground (865bb52c). public/data/folio-highres.json ends at 2026-W44, so W45 has not opened. The calendar demo is still linked only from design/experiments/ and design/experiments/folios/; /design/folios/ does not link it.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:24] probe — wonder_folio_worktable_calendar: the October page (design/folios/october-2026/) has no calendar and lays the month out by kind (folios, panels, cutouts, pads, ask); the calendar demo still lays out September's thirty-one as "October, one folio a day". The question moves from which order to whether a month becomes a calendar at all.
 >>[2026-11-06 12:28] plan — PLAN.md's audit and first public slice, answered by the release shelf, folded into one kept-rules line; five named next slices, four of them the creator's. Proposal (slice 4): a folio's popover names the page it opens, so the shelf is a door as well as a display.
 >>[2026-11-10 11:14] note — lore-land-plans.spw#value: a folio says where it opens. The price spell stays lore.land's f8. Marks stay out of inventory. 2026-W45's five stay next.
}

^"open"{
 calendar = ~"./wip.spw#wonder_folio_worktable_calendar"
 primes = "Does the primes demo's scan-order walk hold before any route shows the set? The creator's call, in a browser (PLAN.md slice 3)."
 week = "Which five open 2026-W45? The creator's call each week (PLAN.md slice 1)."
 offer = "Which forms, prices and shipping does a first folio sale carry? The creator's call; sales stay closed until then."
 first_request = "Has a request arrived through the #folio-request card yet? Only the creator can say."
}

^"cache"{
 ~#status: "waiting"
 ~#next_commit: "+[folios] Open 2026-W45's high-res five, once the creator names them"
 ~#files_hot: "public/data/folio-highres.json, design/folios/index.html, design/folios/october-2026/index.html, design/experiments/folios/calendar/index.html"
 ~#gate: "the creator names the week's five; the calendar and the primes demo wait on the creator's look (#>wonder_folio_worktable_calendar)"
 ~#last_stream: "2026-11-10"
}

#>wonder_folio_worktable_calendar
?["Should October's calendar keep scan order or take chosen days, and live as a site page or a printable sheet?"]{
  #:depth #!experiential ~#lens(comparison)
  ~#with: @plan @calendar
  ~#taste: "A month of folios is a walk before it is a grid; the order is part of what was made."
  ~#hypothesis: "Scan order shows the month as it was made; chosen days show it as it should be read."
  ~#tension: "The review was worth most before October ended, and October has passed unreviewed. The October drop now has its own page (design/folios/october-2026/, 2c95bf13), which lays the month out by kind rather than by day, so the demo may have been overtaken, or it may be the form a later month takes."
  ~#expect: "At pocket, scan order reads as a sequence a reader follows; a printable sheet asks for chosen days."
  ~#unblocks: "hanging October's calendar from the folio shelf"
  ~#probe(read)
  !probe{ "open /design/experiments/folios/calendar/ at pocket and at desktop beside /design/folios/, and say which order a reader follows without help" }
  $%[calendar.scan_order, calendar.chosen_days, calendar.sheet, calendar.retire]
}
